{"status":"completed","summary":"node1 now synchronizes with pool.ntp.org through chronyd, and synchronization remains healthy after a verified node restart.","actions_performed":["Backed up and updated /etc/chrony.conf to use `pool pool.ntp.org iburst`.","Validated the configuration and enabled/restarted chronyd.","Verified direct source selection and synchronized clock state.","Restarted node1 and confirmed its boot ID changed.","Canceled a redundant fallback reboot schedule and confirmed no second restart occurred."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Configure synchronization with pool.ntp.org","command_ids":["cmd-954c5fb44a6c40dc","cmd-93e4301e73f94e43","cmd-a37239270e99445b"],"summary":"The persistent configuration names pool.ntp.org, parses successfully, and chronyd selected a pool.ntp.org source."},{"requirement":"Keep synchronization active across restarts","command_ids":["cmd-bcefa4dd964340a1","cmd-754422b58967463d","cmd-d71c48b0180c4f34"],"summary":"Before and after restart, chronyd is enabled and active. Post-restart checks show NTPSynchronized=yes, the persisted pool configuration, and pool.ntp.org as the selected source."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-bcefa4dd964340a1","cmd-708f4117b373421c","cmd-754422b58967463d","cmd-d71c48b0180c4f34"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 8c28f3cd-ef9b-4edb-b26e-9a7a6f76c879 was captured, the reboot was acknowledged, and recovered boot ID 97c7f199-0bf5-4e07-bfce-6e2b1f211942 proves the node restarted. Final health remained stable."},{"requirement":"Redundant reboot prevention","command_ids":["cmd-320eb3645a4b4938","cmd-55761e41443a42ce","cmd-d71c48b0180c4f34"],"summary":"A fallback reboot was scheduled only after the first reboot had already completed; it was immediately canceled. A check beyond its former deadline confirmed the boot ID remained unchanged and chronyd stayed healthy."}]}
